    'The way to run this on a schedule is cron. It runs when you say it runs, it leaves a log, and it does not depend on anybody visiting the site. A nightly incremental scan reads only what has changed since the last one, and the checking is incremental for free, because a verdict is only asked again once it has gone stale.' => 'The way to run this on a schedule is cron. It runs when you say it runs, it leaves a log, and it does not depend on anybody visiting the site. A nightly incremental scan reads only what has changed since the last one, and the checking is incremental for free, because a verdict is only asked again once it has gone stale.',
    'The website answered each of these with a 404 or a 410, the codes for a page that is not there any more, or the link failed enough times in a row to be counted as gone. Anybody clicking one of them lands nowhere, so put the right address in or take the link out.' => 'The website answered each of these with a 404 or a 410, the codes for a page that is not there any more, or the link failed enough times in a row to be counted as gone. Anybody clicking one of them lands nowhere, so put the right address in or take the link out.',
    'There is no need to work through a list this size from the top. Start with these and it comes down quicker.' => 'There is no need to work through a list this size from the top. Start with these and it comes down quicker.',
    'These all still work, so nobody is landing on an error. URL is the address as it is written in your content, and Goes To is where the server actually sends anybody who follows it. A permanent one is worth tidying up anyway: the page it points at has moved for good and your content is still carrying the old address. Copy what is in the Goes To column into the link and it stops being a detour.' => 'These all still work, so nobody is landing on an error. URL is the address as it is written in your content, and Goes To is where the server actually sends anybody who follows it. A permanent one is worth tidying up anyway: the page it points at has moved for good and your content is still carrying the old address. Copy what is in the Goes To column into the link and it stops being a detour.',
    'These broke recently, so whatever changed is still fresh in somebody\'s mind.' => 'These broke recently, so whatever changed is still fresh in somebody\'s mind.',
    'These did not answer when last checked: a server that was down, or an address that would not resolve. They are retried on their own, and one that keeps failing is called Broken after a few failures in a row.' => 'These did not answer when last checked: a server that was down, or an address that would not resolve. They are retried on their own, and one that keeps failing is called Broken after a few failures in a row.',
    'These did not answer when they were asked: a server that was down or an address that would not resolve. They are tried again on their own, and one that keeps failing moves to Broken. Nothing to do here unless you already know a link is wrong.' => 'These did not answer when they were asked: a server that was down or an address that would not resolve. They are tried again on their own, and one that keeps failing moves to Broken. Nothing to do here unless you already know a link is wrong.',
    'These refused an automated check. LinkedIn and sites behind Cloudflare are the usual ones. They are most likely grand in a real browser, so they are never counted as broken.' => 'These refused an automated check. LinkedIn and sites behind Cloudflare are the usual ones. They are most likely grand in a real browser, so they are never counted as broken.',
    'This is the only way to catch what a template hard-codes: the footer, the main nav, the widget somebody dropped into a layout years ago. None of that is in anybody\'s content, so nothing else in a scan will ever see it. It costs one request per page against your own server, so keep the page cap sensible and leave this off if your site is very large or the server is tight.' => 'This is the only way to catch what a template hard-codes: the footer, the main nav, the widget somebody dropped into a layout years ago. None of that is in anybody\'s content, so nothing else in a scan will ever see it. It costs one request per page against your own server, so keep the page cap sensible and leave this off if your site is very large or the server is tight.',
    'This one is being left alone. It is kept out of every list and never checked, until somebody puts it back.' => 'This one is being left alone. It is kept out of every list and never checked, until somebody puts it back.',
    'This run was stopped before it finished. The counts cover what it got through.' => 'This run was stopped before it finished. The counts cover what it got through.',
